- “Should I have a stress test or ambulatory monitor based on my symptoms/history?”
- “Is my anticoagulation (apixaban) and metoprolol dose appropriate — or should cardiology review?”

Suggested wording to use at the visit or in message to Dr. Wilson
- Short script to request DEXA/FRAX/labs: “I have a history of osteopenia and diabetes. Could we order a DEXA scan and labs (25‑OH vitamin D, calcium, creatinine, TSH) and calculate my FRAX score so we can decide if I need treatment?”
- Short script to request cardiology evaluation: “Given my diabetes and my medications (apixaban, metoprolol), could you review whether I should be referred to Colorado Cardiology? If helpful, please start with a baseline ECG and echocardiogram and then advise on referral.”

Other annual-visit items to confirm
- Eye exam for diabetic retinopathy (ideally yearly). Ask whether recent ophthalmology/retina visit is on record.
- A1C confirmation and current target/treatment plan.
- Lipids, kidney testing (eGFR/urine albumin), blood pressure control, vaccination updates (flu, shingles, Covid, pneumococcal if indicated).
- Review of fall risk and home safety, especially if on anticoagulation.

