- Type 2 diabetes increases fracture risk independent of BMD — clinicians often use FRAX with caution and may be more likely to treat earlier. Good glycemic control and neuropathy/vision checks help reduce falls.
- Retinopathy means extra attention to fall prevention, regular ophthalmology follow-up, and balance/gait evaluation.

