Osteopenia / bone health — what to consider and ask
- Why we’re worried: Age, diabetes, certain meds (long‑term PPI use), and history of retinopathy (higher fall risk from vision loss) can raise fracture risk even if BMD is borderline.
- Tests to ask for:
  - DEXA scan (if you don’t have a recent one). If you haven’t had one and you have risk factors (T2D, steroid use, low BMI, prior fragility fracture), consider baseline DEXA now.
